      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If you disable the node, what happens to the node after it? Like if you have 3 nodes, with a noodle flowing through them... and you disable the middle node.. does the 3rd node still get executed? Or do you want a chain reaction, where disabling a node, stops all further execution in the noodle flow? If the latter is the case, then simply removing the flow noodle accomplishes the same thing as disabling a node, doesn't it?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5dfa8799c6c3555dc03bf5c0",
      "author": {
        "_id": "58c6cbcffd04b1785f747b6c",
